# ===========================================================================
#  voice.cmds  -  starpOS voice command registry
# ===========================================================================
#  Every phrase the voice engine listens for. voice.ps1 builds its speech
#  recognition grammar straight out of this file, so adding a new spoken
#  command means adding one line here. No code to change.
#
#  FORMAT:  phrase|action|target|spoken reply
#
#    phrase  what you say. Keep it short, two or three words recognise best.
#    action  say   - just speak the reply
#            run   - speak the reply, then launch target
#            show  - speak the reply, then print the text file in target
#            list  - speak the reply, then list the folder in target
#            exit  - speak the reply, then close the voice engine
#    target  the file or folder the action needs, or blank for say and exit
#    reply   what starpOS speaks back
#
#  Phrases are matched without case. Do not use the | character in a reply.
# ===========================================================================

starpOS|say||Yes Boss. I am listening. All starp O S core systems are online.
hello|say||Hello. starp O S is running and ready for your instructions.
who are you|say||I am starp O S, built by the Scott Soft team.
what time is it|say||Check the desktop header. The clock is in the top bar.

open file|list|..|Opening file explorer.
open system|list|.|Listing the system folder.
show help|show|help.txt|Opening the help screen.
show errors|show|errors.txt|Opening the error code reference.
show notes|list|..\data\notes|Listing your saved notes.

system info|run|sysinfo.ps1|Reading the real machine specifications.
open desktop|run|startup.bat|Returning to the starp O S desktop.
open movies|run|movies.bat|Opening the movie theater.
open usb|run|usb.bat|Opening the U S B device controller.
task manager|run|tasklist|Listing the running processes.

exit|exit||Exiting voice control system.
shut down|exit||Shutting down the voice engine. Goodbye.
